<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 54,775 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 54,775 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 54,775 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday, compared to 33,440 tonnes on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Wednesday	 Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			25,945	    15,398</p>
<p>    Import cargo			28,830	    18,042</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, one ship was expected to sail and five were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>High speed deisel    73,000	 Chesapeak City     25/2</p>
<p>Furnace oil	    60,000	 Al-Safa		25/2</p>
<p>Rock phosphate	 27,000	 Philadelphia	  4/3</p>
<p>High speed deisel    56,000	 Al-Maqwa		due</p>
<p>Palm oil		 16,500	 Bunga Cenderawasih 28/2</p>
<p>Chemicals		 9,900	 Ncc Najd		1/3</p>
<p>Fertilizer	     10,200	 Ever More Clear    26/2</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
